Bugfix: Return 404 again for a PROPFIND on a missing path

Since 10.16.5, a PROPFIND request on a path that does not exist, or on a
create-only share, returned a malformed 207 Multi-Status response instead of
404 Not Found. The sabre/event update in 10.16.5 changed the order in which
listeners of equal priority run, so the Sabre DAV httpPropFind handler ran
before the checkPropFind check. checkPropFind now has a higher priority, so it
always runs first.

